= Ecosystem — Technical =

== Stocks, transfers and boundaries ==
An ecosystem model may represent living biomass, soil pools, dissolved nutrients and abiotic compartments as stocks, with transfer rates among them. The mathematical balance for a chosen stock is incoming flux minus outgoing flux plus or minus internal conversion terms as appropriate.

== Trophic structure ==
Food webs represent multiple feeding pathways and energy transfer among trophic roles. A food chain is a simplified linear pathway; real consumers may feed across several levels. Primary production, respiration, decomposition and export affect the energy and matter budgets.

== Disturbance and observation ==
Ecosystem condition cannot be inferred from species count alone. Diversity, composition, function, nutrient stocks, net carbon exchange and resilience may change in different directions. A repeated measurement requires consistent sampling boundaries, detection effort, temporal coverage and uncertainty.

